# Process 11, the previews handler that portal.WithPreviews returns: its
# answer to each request from the HTTP server, previews.ServeHTTP, which runs
# boxes 11.1 to 11.4 in order. The published portal handler, in docportal the
# reloader of box 9, and the previews configuration's Open and access hook
# are the receiver's fields, fixed at box 11 of flow.dfd. The response writer
# passes unchanged from the HTTP server to box 11.4. Box 11.3 calls Open,
# which in docportal is source.Previews.Handler: it finds the folder's
# snapshot in the preview snapshots, or loads it from the bucket folder at
# the folder's first request, on a context that no request ends, and drops
# the least recently used snapshot beyond the preview limit; a failed load
# of a folder with objects stays there for the refresh interval. Each
# preview folder in memory has a reloader of its own, process 9, whose
# checks list the folder through a listing that drops the snapshot from the
# preview snapshots when it finds the folder empty; a timer drops a snapshot
# unused for the idle time. These drops run inside source.Previews, behind
# Open, so no box of this diagram draws them.
# Box 11.4 sends the request on to the preview's portal handler or to the
# published one, with the banner in the request's context, for the pages of
# box 3.4.3, where a page with the notice clears the notice cookie.
# By hand: dfd --box 300x150 --per-row 5 --number --number-prefix 11. docs/flow.11.dfd -o flow.11.svg

{HTTP server}
> request
[11.1. Read what the request asks of the previews: to leave the preview at /previews/, to switch to the folder named in a longer /previews/ path, with the path to open after the switch, the reader's preview from the preview cookie, and an ended preview from the notice cookie
 (portal.readPreviewRequest)]
> request, preview request
[11.2. Ask the access hook for the access of the request's reader, once, for a request with a folder to switch to or a preview to serve, and never for a request to leave: Everything without a hook, and an access that allows nothing after an error or a nil access, whose cause goes to the log
 (portal.previews.readerAccess)]
    > request
    < access, error
    <Embedding program>
    > hook problem
    <Log>
> request, preview request, access
[11.3. Open the portal handler of the request's folder, the one to switch to, else the reader's preview, for a reader whose access allows that preview, and none for a request to leave: an error for an invalid name, a folder hidden from the reader, a missing folder, or a failed load
 (portal.previews.openFolder)]
    > folder
    < allowed
    <Embedding program>
    < preview snapshot
    > preview snapshot
    |Preview snapshots|
    > keys
    < listing, files
    <Bucket folder>
> response writer, request, preview request, portal handler, open error
[11.4. Answer the request: leave the preview, or switch to the opened folder with a redirect that sets the preview cookie; send it to the preview's portal handler with the banner, or after a failure to the published portal handler with the notice or the 404 page of the folder; send a request with the notice cookie alone to the published portal handler with the notice; each of these privately; and send a request with neither cookie, unchanged, to the published portal handler
 (portal.previews.send)]
    > load problem
    <Log>
    > response
    <HTTP server>

# type: request = *net/http.Request
# type: preview request = portal.previewRequest
# type: access = portal.Access
# type: error = error
# type: hook problem = error
# type: folder = string
# type: allowed = bool
# type: keys = []string
# type: listing = source.Listing
# type: files = [][]byte
# type: response writer = net/http.ResponseWriter
# type: portal handler = net/http.Handler
# type: open error = error
# type: load problem = error
# type: response = []byte
